md`# brain-core

The Worker every other Worker is bound to. It routes a method or a path to the Worker of the service that declared it, and keeps what must last: the notebook-side rows, the route table and the rules the owner sets.

It answers bindings only. A caller is who the kernel says it is, and the kernel is known by its key; any other Worker is \`worker:NAME\`, whatever it claims.

| answer | when |
|---|---|
| 403 \`Forbidden\` | A Worker calls a method that its service did not declare in \`calls\` (mode \`enforce\`). A member's Worker calls outside its author's reach, or is switched off. A rule cannot be decided. |
| 405 \`InvalidRequest\` | A query sent as POST, or a procedure sent as GET. |
| 400 \`InvalidRequest\` | A query parameter is given two times. A rule and a price read the last of them and a service may read the first, so the call is refused. |
| 401 \`AuthRequired\` | The rule of the method or path is not true for this caller. |
| 429 \`RateLimitExceeded\` | A member's calls for the day are used. |
| 402 \`OutOfCredits\` | The method has a price and the account that pays has less than the price left for the day, or the call has no account. |
| 402 \`PriceOverCeiling\` | The price of this call is more than one call may cost. |
| 501 \`MethodNotImplemented\` | No service declares the method. |
| 502 \`UpstreamUnavailable\` | The Worker of the service that declares it is not bound to the core. |

| method | |
|---|---|
| \`service.list\` | query, anyone. \`{ services: [{ worker, role, module, hash, verified, methods, paths, secrets }] }\`: every Worker but a member's. |
| \`service.register\`, \`service.unregister\`, \`service.health\` | procedure, the deployer. The route and the key of a Worker it deployed or removed (removal also deletes that Worker's settings), and the health of a Worker with no address. |
| \`deploy.report\` | procedure, owner. \`{ worker, hash, ok, tests: [{ name, ok }], reason }\`: the page's verdict after it ran the module's tests. 409 when that hash is not running. |
| \`rows.get\`, \`rows.list\` | query, owner. \`?worker=&key=\`, \`?worker=&prefix=\`: the notebook-side rows kept for a Worker name. |
| \`rows.put\`, \`rows.delete\` | procedure, owner. \`{ worker, key, value }\`, \`{ worker, key }\`. |
| \`rule.list\` | query, owner. The rules the owner set. |
| \`rule.put\`, \`rule.delete\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ target, allow }\`: a CEL expression in place of the rule a service declared. A rule the service fixed is refused. |
| \`calls.list\` | query, owner. \`{ mode, implicit, undeclared: [{ worker, method, n }] }\`. |
| \`calls.setMode\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ mode: "report" | "enforce" | null, clear }\`. |
| \`config.list\` | query, the owner's own session. \`{ workers: [{ worker, values }], protected, ttl }\`: every stored setting. |
| \`config.get\` | query, the owner's own session. \`?worker=\`. \`{ worker, values, changes, read }\`. \`changes\`: the last 100, each \`{ at, by, key, old, value }\`. \`read\`: the keys one running instance of the Worker has read from \`config\`, each with its value and \`from\`: \`deploy\`, \`stored\` or \`unset\`. |
| \`config.set\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ worker, key, value }\`. A number, a boolean or text of at most 500 characters; \`null\` removes the key. At most 50 keys for a Worker, and 8 KB as they are sent (URL-encoded JSON). |
| \`GET /llms.txt\` | anyone. Text for a program: how to call this Brain, how the owner makes a token, and one line for each method and path of each service, written from \`config.host\` and the route table on each request. It points at \`getSource?worker=NAME&part=reference\` for what a method takes and answers. A member's Worker and what the owner set in place of a rule or price are left out, and so are the methods of the kernel, the core and the deployer: the file says where their references are. |
| \`price.list\` | query, owner. \`{ prices: [{ target, worker, declared, set, setAt }], unit, defaults }\`. |
| \`price.put\`, \`price.delete\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ target, price }\`: a CEL expression in place of the price a service declared. |
| \`quota.get\` | query, any account. \`{ who, day, spent, daily, remaining, resetsAt }\` for the caller's own account. The owner reads another with \`?who=\`. |
| \`quota.list\`, \`quota.ledger\` | query, owner. Each account's day, and the charges of one day (\`?day=&who=&limit=\`) with totals by account and by method. |
| \`quota.put\`, \`quota.setDefaults\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ who, daily }\`, and \`{ owner, member, worker, token, perCall, keepDays }\`. \`null\` is the default again. |
| \`delegation.create\` | procedure, the owner's or a member's own session. \`{ name, holder: { worker }, scope, until, daily, note }\` → the record, with its \`id\`. With \`holder: { secret: true }\` and \`caps\` (the owner only) the answer has \`secret\`, once: a token. The kernel's \`token.create\` and a sign-in link make these. |
| \`delegation.resolve\`, \`delegation.adopt\` | procedures, the kernel. \`{ sha256 }\` of a secret → \`{ delegation }\` or null; and a token from before 2026-10-10, handed over by its hash. |
| \`delegation.list\`, \`delegation.revoke\` | query and procedure, the same callers. The owner reads and revokes any, a member their own. \`{ id }\`. |

**Delegations** (design: \`plan/cloud-brain-authority.md\`; built 2026-10-10 for a Worker holder only). The owner or a member lets a Worker the owner deployed call the methods in a \`scope\`, until a time or until it is revoked. The Worker names the delegation on a call it makes:

\`\`\`js
xrpc.fetch("com.lopecode.brain.m.0a1b.shop.receive", { method: "POST", headers: { "x-brain-as": id, "x-brain-hops": String(hops), "content-type": "application/json" }, body })
\`\`\`

- The call is then by who made the delegation: \`caller\` in a rule, the account that pays. \`caller.delegation\` is the id and \`caller.holder\` is \`worker:NAME\`. It is not their own tab: \`caller.session\` is false, and a browser or a container it makes is kept under \`d:<id>\`.
- It is allowed when the method is in the scope and the maker may call it at that moment. A revoked delegation, an ended one or a removed member is refused within 5 s, the time a core instance remembers a row.
- It reaches no \`infra\`, \`secret\`, \`token\`, \`grant\`, \`people\` or \`delegation\` method, and no method of the owner's own session, whatever the scope says. It is not held to the Worker's own \`calls\`.
- It begins a chain of its own: the origin is the maker, and the origin of whatever the Worker was answering is not read. \`x-brain-hops\` says how long the chain already is; the core adds one, sends it on with each forwarded call, and refuses a chain over 8.
- \`daily\` is the most the chain may spend in a UTC day, counted beside the maker's own allowance. \`delegation.list\` shows \`spentToday\`. Calls made at the same moment can pass it by the price of those calls; the maker's allowance is exact.
- A member's delegations are deleted when the member is removed.
- A secret holder (a token made from 2026-10-10) sends the secret to the kernel as \`Authorization: Bearer\`. Its calls are the owner's: the owner's rules and allowance, \`caller.holder\` is \`secret:NAME\` and \`caller.token\` is \`NAME\`. It is the owner's own tab only with the cap \`session\`, and then only for a method the scope names by its name or a prefix: \`*\` alone does not reach \`rule.put\`, \`config.set\` or any method whose rule is \`caller.session\`. When a call is not the owner's tab, what it makes in a store is kept under \`d:<id>\`. \`deploy\` and \`unattended\` are read by the kernel for \`infra.*\`.
- A holder that takes a delegation's id from a caller must check that the caller made it (\`from\`). An id is not a secret.

**Origin.** A rule reads \`caller\`, who made the call, and \`origin\`, who started the chain of calls it is part of. The two have the same fields. For a call from outside they are equal. When a Worker makes a call while it answers one, \`caller\` is the Worker and \`origin\` is the origin of the call it answers. A call a Worker makes by its own schedule has the Worker as \`origin\`. For a member's Worker \`caller\` is its author, and so is \`origin\` when it answers nobody.

\`\`\`js
app.post(NS + "publish", async (c) => xrpc.procedure("com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.putRecord", record))
// the rule of bluesky.putRecord
'caller.session || (caller.worker == "brain-x-feed" && origin.kind == "owner")'
\`\`\`

The core sends a reference with each call it forwards (\`x-brain-context\`): the origin, the Worker it is for and an end time 120 s later, signed with HMAC-SHA-256 under a key that is one of the core's rows. The Worker wrapper (\`workerRuntime\` in \`@tomlarkworthy/cloudflare-iac\`) holds it while the Worker answers that call and sends it back with each call the Worker makes to the core in that time: \`xrpc\`, \`secrets\`, \`sql\`, \`inbox\`. On Cloudflare it is held in \`AsyncLocalStorage\`, so two calls answered at once keep their own. Until 2026-10-07 a service passed it on by hand (\`behalf\`, removed). The core reads a reference only from a Worker known by its key, and only one made for that Worker and not ended. Any other reference is ignored and the origin is the Worker. A Worker can use a reference again until it ends. The core also sends \`x-brain-origin\` and \`x-brain-origin-via\` in clear, for a Worker that decides rules of its own.

A rule that does not name \`origin\` lets the Worker act for anyone it answers. \`origin.trusted\` is true for the owner, a token, and an account the kernel passed for the first method of the chain. A rule of a secret or a table reads the same \`origin\`. A Worker holds a secret's value for 5 s for one origin, and asks again for another.

| call | rule reads origin | why |
|---|---|---|
| feed → \`bluesky.putRecord\`, \`bluesky.deleteRecord\` | yes | the record is public |
| inbox → \`*.send\` | no | the reply goes only to the address the entry came from |
| library → \`static.put\`, \`static.get\`, \`static.delete\` | no | the library decides who reads a notebook |
| whatsapp → \`static.put\` | no | a picture that arrived, with no caller |
| bluesky, whatsapp → \`lease.get\`, \`inbox.append\` | no | started by the Worker's own clock |
| any → \`secret.get\`, \`db.sql\` | no | the Worker's own secrets and tables |

**Settings** (added 2026-10-09). A value a service reads from \`config\` and gives a default (\`config.pollMs ?? 30000\`) can be stored here, per Worker, and is read with no deploy. A service does nothing to take part: the core sends a Worker's stored settings with each call it forwards (\`x-brain-settings\`), and the Worker wrapper shows them through \`config\`. The core reads the rows at most once in 60 s for one instance, so a call forwarded more than 60 s after a change carries it. A run by the clock (a Worker with a schedule) has no call to read them from: it uses the copy the Worker last had, and reads the row itself only when that copy is 5 minutes old. So a tick may run on a setting up to 5 minutes old. Reading the row on every tick was not done: it is one database statement a tick, at rest. Removing a Worker deletes its settings and their log.

\`\`\`
brain.ts curl /xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.config.set --owner -X POST -d '{"worker":"brain-x-inbox","key":"pollMs","value":60000}'
\`\`\`

What a setting cannot do. A key the deployer bound at deploy (\`owner\`, \`host\`, \`base\`, \`subdomain\`, \`account\`, \`deployer\`) is never replaced by a stored value: the wrapper reads the bound one first. \`config.set\` refuses those names, and six more that the kernel, the core and the deployer read, with 400. The kernel, the core and the deployer take no stored settings. Access rules, prices, approval and keys are not settings. A setting is written to the log in clear: do not store a secret in one. Rows: \`config/<worker>\` (the values) and \`config-log/<worker>\` (the changes).

**Prices and credits** (added 2026-10-08). A method or a path can have a price beside its rule: a CEL expression over the same \`caller\`, \`origin\` and \`request\`, which gives US dollars. The owner's price (\`price.put\`) stands in for the declared one. A call with no price, or a price of 0, reads the route table and the settings the core already holds and writes no row.

\`\`\`js
"com.lopecode.brain.shop.time": { type: "procedure", who: "owner", price: "double(request.params.seconds) * 0.000025" }
\`\`\`

The order is rule, price, charge, forward. The price is for the Worker's own work: a method it calls is charged by its own price when the call reaches the core. A price that throws, is not a number, or is less than 0 refuses the call with 403; one above \`perCall\` refuses it with 402. A price reads the query of the request and not its body, as a rule does.

| the call is started by | the account that pays | default a day |
|---|---|---|
| the owner's session, the owner's turn, the owner's PDS, the token of a sign-in link made with \`unattended\` | \`owner\` | $1.00 |
| a member's session, PDS, portal or turn | \`did:…\`, the member | $0.10 |
| a turn in a room | the person who wrote the message, as any turn | |
| a token (a delegation with a secret holder), a Worker calling under the owner's delegation | \`owner\`, and no more than the delegation's \`daily\` | $1.00 |
| a Worker by its own clock | \`worker:NAME\` | $0.10 |
| a member's Worker by its own clock | its author | |
| nobody (\`anonymous\`) | none: a priced call is refused | |

A Worker that answers a call spends the credits of that call's origin, through any number of Workers. The most one call may cost is $1. An account's day starts at 00:00 UTC.

A priced call is charged when the core accepts it, before it is forwarded. The charge is not returned: not when the Worker answers an error, and not when it throws. A service whose call can fail after the charge gives its price to one method that does only the purchase. The answer to a priced call carries \`x-brain-price\`, what was charged.

An account's day is one row, \`spend/DAY/ACCOUNT\`: a list that each charge is appended to in one statement. A charge counts when the charges that count before it, and it, are inside the allowance it was made under. The list alone decides that, so calls made at once do not spend past the allowance and no call holds a lock. A charge that lost to another made at the same time stays in the list and counts for nothing. A priced call is two statements (append, read). A day holds 2000 charges that count for one account; the next is refused. Spending only grows in a day, so a core that read an account as spent refuses it with no write until the day ends or the allowance grows. Days older than \`keepDays\` (30) are deleted at the first priced call of a UTC day; a Brain with no priced call keeps its rows until the next one.

Limits. A cost known only after the call, such as the tokens of a model call, has no method yet: a price is fixed before the call and nothing brings it down afterwards (Tom, 2026-10-08: no refunds), so it needs a design of its own. The allowance of a member's calls for a day (429) is a separate count.

**Calls.** A Worker calls the methods its service lists in \`calls\`. The core reads the list from the Worker's \`getInfo\`, which the deployer bound at deploy, and keeps it for that deployed hash. A name is exact. \`*\` is one part of a name; as the last part it is one or more: \`com.lopecode.brain.static.*\`, \`com.lopecode.brain.*.send\`. A list of only \`*\` matches nothing.

Three methods are not listed, because a platform cell calls them: \`secret.get\` (\`secrets\`), \`db.sql\` (\`sql\`) and \`inbox.append\` (\`inbox\`). Each has its own rule.

The kernel and the deployer are not checked: they are not Workers of a service. A member's Worker is not checked against a list either. The deployer writes \`calls: []\` for it, and each of its calls is checked as its author (see Members).

In mode \`report\` an undeclared call is counted and passed. In mode \`enforce\` it is refused. The default in the code is \`report\`; a Brain is in \`enforce\` after the owner sets it. At most 200 names are counted.`
// %%
core_service = cloudflare.Service("core", coreApp, { role: "core" })
// %%
// Announced to the page, so the Services list shows it. A cell of its own: a deployed function cannot depend on it.
core_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", core_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced core_service";
}
// %%
coreApp = {
  const app = new hono.Hono();
  const NS = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.";
  const fail = (c, status, error, message) => (c.set("error", error), c.json({ error, message }, status));
  const keys = new Map();
  // What the core forwards to: recipes, and system Workers such as the database.
  const routed = (r) => r.role === "recipe" || r.role === "system" || r.role === "member";
  const identify = async (request) => {
    const url = new URL(request.url);
    // From the internet only the deployer gets this far, and the wrapper has named it.
    if (!url.hostname.endsWith(".internal")) return { caller: ["deployer", "guard"].includes(request.headers.get("x-brain-caller")) ? "deployer" : "anonymous" }; // "guard": a wrapper from before 2026-10-08
    const key = request.headers.get("x-brain-key");
    if (!key) return { caller: "anonymous" };
    const hash = await sha256(key);
    if (!keys.has(hash)) {
      const known = await rows.get("key/" + hash);
      if (known) keys.set(hash, known);
    }
    const known = keys.get(hash);
    if (!known) return { caller: "anonymous" };
    // A member's Worker is known by its key like any other, and is then checked as its author.
    if (known.role === "member") return { caller: "worker:" + known.worker, keyed: known.worker, member: { worker: known.worker, author: known.author } };
    if (known.role !== "kernel") return { caller: "worker:" + known.worker, keyed: known.worker };
    return { caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller") || "anonymous", via: request.headers.get("x-brain-via") || "", kernel: true };
  };
  // Origin. The caller of a call is who made it; the origin is who started the chain of calls it is part of. With
  // each call the core forwards goes a reference: the origin, the Worker it is for and when it ends, signed with a
  // key only the core holds (HMAC-SHA-256; the key is one of the core's own rows, made at first use). A Worker that
  // sends the reference back on a call it makes is given that origin. A reference that is absent, changed, ended or
  // made for another Worker gives nothing, and the origin is then the Worker itself. Nothing a Worker says in clear
  // is read. Signed and not kept: the core has many instances and none of them remembers a call.
  const CONTEXT_MS = 120000;
  // Is this the caller's own tab: a person's session. A call under a delegation says so itself (who.tab).
  const tabOf = (who) => (typeof who.tab === "boolean" ? who.tab : who.via === "session");
  const utf8 = new TextEncoder();
  const b64u = (bytes) => btoa(String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(bytes))).replace(/\+/g, "-").replace(/\//g, "_").replace(/=+$/, "");
  const unb64u = (text) => Uint8Array.from(atob(text.replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/")), (ch) => ch.charCodeAt(0));
  let originKey = null;
  const keyOfOrigin = () =>
    (originKey ??= (async () => {
      if (!(await rows.get("origin-key"))) await rows.putIfAbsent("origin-key", b64u(crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32))));
      return crypto.subtle.importKey("raw", utf8.encode(await rows.get("origin-key")), { name: "HMAC", hash: "SHA-256" }, false, ["sign", "verify"]);
    })().catch((e) => {
      originKey = null;
      throw e;
    }));
  const contextFor = async (worker, origin) => {
    // t: the origin's own tab. d, n, h: the delegation the chain began under, who holds it, and how long the chain is.
    const payload = b64u(utf8.encode(JSON.stringify({ o: origin.caller, v: origin.via || "", w: worker, e: Date.now() + (config.contextMs ?? CONTEXT_MS), t: tabOf(origin) ? 1 : 0, d: origin.d || "", n: origin.holder || "", h: origin.hops || 0 })));
    return "c1." + payload + "." + b64u(await crypto.subtle.sign("HMAC", await keyOfOrigin(), utf8.encode(payload)));
  };
  const originFrom = async (reference, worker) => {
    const m = /^c1\.([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)\.([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)$/.exec(reference || "");
    if (!m) return null;
    try {
      // One spelling for each signature: base64url has spare bits in its last character.
      if (b64u(unb64u(m[2])) !== m[2] || !(await crypto.subtle.verify("HMAC", await keyOfOrigin(), unb64u(m[2]), utf8.encode(m[1])))) return null;
      const p = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(unb64u(m[1])));
      // A reference from before 2026-10-10 has no t: the tab is then the via, as it was.
      return p.w === worker && p.e > Date.now() && typeof p.o === "string" ? { caller: p.o, via: p.v || "", tab: p.t === undefined ? p.v === "session" : !!p.t, d: p.d || "", holder: p.n || "", hops: p.h || 0 } : null;
    } catch {
      return null;
    }
  };
  // A method as it is logged: the name after com.lopecode.brain., or the path a service declared.
  // A name nobody declared is logged as one, "(unknown)", and not as what a stranger typed.
  // Declared: a service's route matched (routeOf), or the core has a handler at this path. Not decided by the status.
  const nameOf = (c) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), nsid = url.pathname.startsWith(NS) ? url.pathname.slice(NS.length) : null;
    const declared = c.get("target") || c.get("routed") || app.routes.some((r) => r.path === url.pathname);
    return declared ? nsid || c.get("path") || url.pathname : "(unknown)";
  };
  const routeOf = async (c) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), nsid = url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/") ? url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/".length) : null;
    // The route table and the owner's rules are read through a few seconds of memory, not from storage on every call.
    for (const route of (await settings.list("route/")).map((r) => r.value).filter(routed)) {
      const method = nsid && route.methods[nsid];
      const path = !nsid && route.paths.find((p) => p.path === url.pathname || (p.path.endsWith("/*") && url.pathname.startsWith(p.path.slice(0, -1))));
      if (!method && !path) continue;
      if (path) c.set("path", path.path);
      c.set("routed", route.worker);
      return { route, method, path, nsid };
    }
    return { nsid };
  };
  // One line a call, in Workers Logs: Cloudflare keeps it 7 days and logs.query reads it. The keys are the ones written
  // here and no others: names and decisions. Never a header, a body, a parameter's value or a secret.
  //   ray     the cf-ray of the call from the internet this one is part of; the kernel passes it on
  //   caller  who called, via how (session, or the member's Worker); origin: who started the chain
  //   delegation, holder   the delegation this call or its chain is under, and the Worker or secret that holds it
  //   worker  the Worker the call was forwarded to, or brain-core
  //   error   the XRPC error name of an answer of 400 and above
  //   price   US dollars, when the method has a price
  //   rule    allow, deny or error; by: what decided. manifest (the service's rule), owner (the owner's rule),
  //           fixed (a rule the service fixed), calls (what a Worker declared), grant (a member's), core (its own methods),
  //           delegation (a call with x-brain-as, or a token's call from the kernel, that was refused)
  const errorOf = (c, res) =>
    c.get("error") || (res.status >= 400 && /json/.test(res.headers.get("content-type") || "") ? res.clone().json().then((b) => (b && typeof b.error === "string" ? b.error.slice(0, 80) : null), () => null) : null);
  const say = async (c, started, status, error) => {
    const who = c.get("who"), origin = c.get("origin") || who, path = new URL(c.req.url).pathname;
    // A method by its name as it is logged (nameOf), so a name nobody declared is "(unknown)" and not what a stranger
    // typed. A path by the pattern a service declared, so what a caller put in a path is not written.
    const nsid = path.startsWith(NS) ? path.slice(NS.length) : null;
    console.log({
      at: "call", ray: (c.req.header("x-brain-ray") || "").slice(0, 64), caller: who.caller, via: who.via || "", origin: origin.caller, delegation: who.d || origin.d || "", holder: who.holder || origin.holder || "",
      method: nsid || c.get("path") ? nameOf(c).slice(0, 80) : "(unknown)", worker: c.get("target") || c.get("routed") || "brain-core", status, error: (await error) || null, ms: Date.now() - started,
      price: c.get("price") ?? null, rule: c.get("rule") || (status === 401 || status === 403 ? "deny" : status < 400 ? "allow" : ""), by: c.get("by") || "core"
    });
  };
  // Members. The kernel hands over who is a member and what each was granted (people.sync), because a Worker
  // cannot ask the kernel. A member's Worker has its author's permissions and no others: a call it makes is
  // allowed when its author is still a member and the method is one of WORKER, a member's own method
  // (com.lopecode.brain.m.…), or in the author's grant. It then goes on as a call by that DID, with the Worker in
  // x-brain-via, so every rule and every store downstream sees the author.
  const WORKER = ["db.sql", "static.put", "static.get", "static.list", "static.tag", "static.setPublic", "static.delete", "blob.upload", "blob.get", "blob.info", "blob.list", "blob.tag", "blob.delete"].map((m) => "com.lopecode.brain." + m);
  const MEMBER_NS = "com.lopecode.brain.m.";
  const QUOTA = { calls: 2000, bytes: 20 * 1024 * 1024, workers: 3 };
  const quotaOf = (person) => ({ ...QUOTA, ...((person && person.quota) || {}) });
  // The day is UTC. clockSkewMs moves it in a test.
  const clock = () => Date.now() + (config.clockSkewMs || 0);
  const today = () => new Date(clock()).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  // Calls into and out of one member's Workers, counted per UTC day.
  const spend = async (person) => (await rows.increment(`mcalls/${person.did}/${today()}`)) <= quotaOf(person).calls;
  const asAuthor = async (c, { worker, author }) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url);
    const nsid = url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/") ? url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/".length) : null;
    const person = await rows.get("person/" + author);
    if (!person) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${author} is not a member, so ${worker} may call nothing`);
    const route = await rows.get("route/" + worker);
    if (!route || route.off) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${worker} is switched off`);
    if (!nsid || !(WORKER.includes(nsid) || nsid.startsWith(MEMBER_NS) || matches(person.methods, nsid))) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${worker} runs as ${author}, who has no grant for ${nsid || url.pathname}`);
    if (!(await spend(person))) return fail(c, 429, "RateLimitExceeded", `${author} has used today's ${quotaOf(person).calls} calls`);
    c.set("who", { caller: author, via: "worker:" + worker });
    return null;
  };
  // Delegations (plan/cloud-brain-authority.md). The owner or a member lets a holder call the methods in a scope:
  // a row delegation/<id>. A Worker that holds one names it in x-brain-as, and the call is then by who made the
  // delegation (`from`): the caller a rule reads, the account that pays. It is not their own tab, and it begins a
  // chain of its own: the origin of whatever the Worker was answering is not read. Allowed when the method is in the
  // scope and `from` may call it now, read on each call through settings' 5 s of memory. Not held to the holder's
  // own `calls`: the scope is the bound.
  const HOPS = 8;
  const mayNow = async (from, nsid) => {
    if (from === "owner") return true;
    const person = from.startsWith("did:") ? await rows.get("person/" + from) : null;
    return !!person && may({ member: true, grant: person.methods }, nsid);
  };
  // What every call under a delegation passes, whoever holds it. null when it stands.
  const stands = async (c, d) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), nsid = url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/") ? url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/".length) : null;
    if (d.until && d.until <= clock()) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `delegation ${d.name} has ended`);
    if (!nsid || neverHeld(nsid) || !matches(d.scope, nsid)) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `delegation ${d.name} does not reach ${nsid || url.pathname}`);
    if (!(await mayNow(d.from, nsid))) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${d.from} may not call ${nsid} now, so delegation ${d.name} does not`);
    return null;
  };
  const asHolder = async (c, worker, id) => {
    const d = /^[0-9a-f]{12}$/.test(id) ? await settings.get("delegation/" + id) : null;
    if (!d || !d.holder || d.holder.worker !== worker) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${worker} holds no such delegation`);
    // The holder says how long the chain is that this call goes on from. A push that causes a push is one longer.
    const hops = Number(c.req.header("x-brain-hops") || 0);
    if (!Number.isInteger(hops) || hops < 0 || hops >= HOPS) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `a chain of calls under delegations is at most ${HOPS} long`);
    const no = await stands(c, d);
    if (no) return no;
    c.set("who", { caller: d.from, via: "delegation:" + d.id, tab: false, holder: "worker:" + worker, d: d.id, hops: hops + 1 });
    return null;
  };
  // A call the kernel passes on for whoever sent a delegation's secret (a token). The kernel matched the secret to
  // the row; the row is read again here and is what decides. It is the maker's own tab when the delegation has the
  // cap `session`, and not otherwise.
  const asSecret = async (c, id) => {
    const d = /^[0-9a-f]{12}$/.test(id) ? await settings.get("delegation/" + id) : null;
    if (!d || !d.holder || !d.holder.secret) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "unknown token");
    const no = await stands(c, d);
    if (no) return no;
    // The cap session holds for what the scope names, by a name or a prefix. A method that only * reaches is not
    // called from the owner's tab: so * does not reach a method of the owner's own session.
    const nsid = new URL(c.req.url).pathname.slice("/xrpc/".length);
    // * is kept as com.lopecode.brain.*, and com.* and com.lopecode.* are the same thing spelled shorter.
    const tab = d.caps.includes("session") && matches(d.scope.filter((m) => !(/[./]\*$/.test(m) && "com.lopecode.brain.".startsWith(m.slice(0, -1)))), nsid);
    c.set("who", { caller: d.from, via: "delegation:" + d.id, tab, holder: "secret:" + d.name, d: d.id, hops: 0 });
    return null;
  };
  // A Worker calls what its service declared in `calls`, and what a platform cell calls for it (IMPLICIT). The list is
  // the Worker's own manifest, which the deployer bound at deploy and the wrapper answers at getInfo before any of the
  // service's code runs. It is held per deployed hash, so a deploy with a new list is followed at once.
  // A name is exact; `*` stands for one part after com.lopecode.brain., and as the last part for one or more:
  // com.lopecode.brain.static.* or com.lopecode.brain.*.send. A path is exact.
  const IMPLICIT = ["secret.get", "db.sql", "inbox.append"].map((m) => "com.lopecode.brain." + m);
  const CALLS_MODE = "report";
  const callMatches = (pattern, name) => {
    const B = "com.lopecode.brain.";
    if (typeof pattern !== "string") return false;
    if (!pattern.includes("*")) return pattern === name;
    if (!pattern.startsWith(B) || !name.startsWith(B)) return false;
    const p = pattern.slice(B.length).split("."), n = name.slice(B.length).split("."), rest = p.at(-1) === "*";
    // A list of only * would be every method.
    if (!p.some((s) => s !== "*")) return false;
    if (rest) p.pop();
    return (rest ? n.length > p.length : n.length === p.length) && p.every((s, i) => s === "*" || s === n[i]);
  };
  const declaredBy = new Map();
  const callsOf = async (worker) => {
    const route = await settings.get("route/" + worker), held = declaredBy.get(worker);
    if (held && route && held.hash === route.hash) return held.calls;
    const short = worker.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "");
    if (!route || !workers.has(short)) return null;
    const r = await workers.fetch(short, new Request(`https://${short}.internal${NS}getInfo`)).catch(() => null);
    const info = r && r.ok ? await r.json().catch(() => null) : null;
    if (!info || !Array.isArray(info.calls)) return null;
    if (info.hash === route.hash) declaredBy.set(worker, { hash: route.hash, calls: info.calls });
    return info.calls;
  };
  // What was called and not declared, counted per Worker and name. At most 200 names are kept, so a Worker cannot grow the table.
  let undeclared = null;
  const note = async (worker, name) => {
    undeclared ??= new Set((await rows.list("undeclared/")).map((r) => r.key));
    const key = "undeclared/" + worker + "/" + name.slice(0, 200);
    if (!undeclared.has(key) && undeclared.size >= 200) return;
    undeclared.add(key);
    await rows.increment(key);
  };
  const callsMode = async () => (await settings.get("calls/mode")) || CALLS_MODE;
  const asDeclared = async (c, worker) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url);
    const name = url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/") ? url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/".length) : url.pathname;
    if (IMPLICIT.includes(name)) return null;
    const calls = await callsOf(worker);
    if ((calls || []).some((p) => callMatches(p, name))) return null;
    await note(worker, name);
    return (await callsMode()) === "enforce" ? fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${worker} did not declare a call to ${name}`) : null;
  };
  app.use("*", async (c, next) => {
    const started = Date.now();
    const who = await identify(c.req.raw);
    c.set("who", who);
    // x-brain-as is read from a Worker known by its key, and not from a member's: that one runs as its author.
    const as = !who.member && who.keyed ? c.req.header("x-brain-as") : null;
    // x-brain-delegation is read from the kernel's key only.
    const token = who.kernel ? c.req.header("x-brain-delegation") : null;
    const no = who.member ? await asAuthor(c, who.member) : as ? await asHolder(c, who.keyed, as) : token ? await asSecret(c, token) : who.caller.startsWith("worker:") ? await asDeclared(c, who.caller.slice("worker:".length)) : null;
    if (no) {
      await routeOf(c);
      c.set("rule", "deny");
      c.set("by", who.member ? "grant" : as || token ? "delegation" : "calls");
      await say(c, started, no.status, c.get("error"));
      return no;
    }
    // Only a Worker known by its key can carry an origin. A member's Worker is checked as its author and keeps the origin too.
    const now = c.get("who");
    c.set("origin", now.d ? now : (who.keyed && (await originFrom(c.req.header("x-brain-context"), who.keyed))) || { caller: now.caller, via: now.via || "" });
    await next();
    const done = say(c, started, c.res.status, errorOf(c, c.res)).catch(() => null);
    try {
      c.executionCtx.waitUntil(done);
    } catch {}
  });
  app.onError((e, c) => fail(c, 500, "InternalServerError", String((e && e.message) || e)));
  // The kernel has already checked a token or a granted DID against the method it named.
  const allowed = (who) => who.caller === "owner" || /^(token|did):/.test(who.caller);
  const owner = async (c, next) => (allowed(c.get("who")) ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner"));
  const session = async (c, next) =>
    c.get("who").caller === "owner" && tabOf(c.get("who")) ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner's own session");
  // A person in their own session: the owner, or a member. The via is the kernel's word, so no Worker and no
  // delegation passes, whatever it holds.
  const inPerson = async (c, next) => {
    const w = c.get("who");
    return w.via === "session" && (w.caller === "owner" || (w.caller.startsWith("did:") && (await rows.get("person/" + w.caller)))) ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner's or a member's own session");
  };
  const deployerOnly = async (c, next) => (c.get("who").caller === "deployer" ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the deployer"));

  const toDeployer = async (verdict) => {
    const r = await deployer.fetch(new Request("https://deployer.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra.verdict", { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }, body: JSON.stringify(verdict) }));
    return r.ok ? r.json() : null;
  };
  // What Workers called without declaring it, and whether such a call is refused or only counted.
  app.get(NS + "calls.list", owner, async (c) =>
    c.json({
      mode: await callsMode(),
      implicit: IMPLICIT,
      undeclared: (await rows.list("undeclared/")).map(({ key, value }) => {
        const [, worker, ...name] = key.split("/");
        return { worker, method: name.join("/"), n: value };
      })
    })
  );
  app.post(NS + "calls.setMode", session, async (c) => {
    const { mode = null, clear = false } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    if (mode !== null && !["report", "enforce"].includes(mode)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "mode is report, enforce or null");
    if (mode === null) await settings.delete("calls/mode");
    else await settings.put("calls/mode", mode);
    if (clear) {
      for (const { key } of await rows.list("undeclared/")) await rows.delete(key);
      undeclared = null;
    }
    return c.json({ mode: await callsMode() });
  });
  // Routes and keys: written by the deployer when it deploys or removes a Worker.
  app.post(NS + "service.register", deployerOnly, async (c) => {
    const r = await c.req.json();
    const was = await rows.get("route/" + r.worker);
    // A deploy is unverified until a page has loaded its module from the Worker and run its tests.
    // The version before keeps its verdict, so a deploy that is put back returns to a version already verified.
    const same = was && r.hash && was.hash === r.hash, back = was && r.hash && was.before && was.before.hash === r.hash;
    const verified = same ? was.verified || null : back ? was.before.verified : null;
    const before = same ? was.before || null : was && was.hash && !back ? { hash: was.hash, verified: was.verified && was.verified.ok ? was.verified : null } : null;
    await settings.put("route/" + r.worker, { worker: r.worker, role: r.role, module: r.module || null, hash: r.hash || null, verified, before, methods: r.methods || {}, paths: r.paths || [], secrets: r.secrets || [], ...(r.role === "member" ? { author: r.author, off: !!(was && was.off) } : {}) });
    await rows.put("key/" + r.keyHash, { worker: r.worker, role: r.role, ...(r.role === "member" ? { author: r.author } : {}) });
    keys.delete(r.keyHash);
    declaredBy.delete(r.worker);
    return c.json({ ok: true });
  });
  app.post(NS + "service.unregister", deployerOnly, async (c) => {
    const { worker } = await c.req.json();
    await settings.delete("route/" + worker);
    for (const { key, value } of await rows.list("key/")) if (value.worker === worker) await rows.delete(key);
    // Its settings go with it: a Worker deployed later under the name starts with none.
    await rows.delete("config/" + worker);
    await rows.delete("config-log/" + worker);
    stored = null;
    keys.clear();
    return c.json({ ok: true });
  });
  // The deployer's health check of a Worker with no address of its own.
  app.post(NS + "service.health", deployerOnly, async (c) => {
    const { worker } = await c.req.json();
    const short = String(worker).replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "");
    if (!workers.has(short)) return c.json({ ok: false, reason: "not bound yet" });
    const r = await workers.fetch(short, new Request(`https://${short}.internal/xrpc/_health`)).catch(() => null);
    return c.json(r && r.ok ? await r.json().catch(() => ({ ok: false })) : { ok: false });
  });
  // Who is a member, what each was granted and their limits: the kernel's table, sent whole each time it changes.
  app.post(NS + "people.sync", async (c) => {
    if (c.get("who").caller !== "kernel") return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the kernel");
    const { people = [] } = await c.req.json();
    const now = new Set(people.map((p) => p.did));
    for (const { key } of await rows.list("person/")) if (!now.has(key.slice("person/".length))) await rows.delete(key);
    // What a removed member delegated goes with them: added again later, they begin with none.
    for (const { value } of await rows.list("delegation/")) if (value.from !== "owner" && !now.has(value.from)) await drop(value);
    for (const p of people) await rows.put("person/" + p.did, { did: p.did, methods: p.methods || [], quota: p.quota || null, tags: p.tags || [] });
    return c.json({ people: people.length });
  });
  // What a member needs to write a service, and how much of each limit is used.
  const idOf = async (did) => (await sha256(did)).slice(0, 10);
  app.get(NS + "member.whoami", async (c) => {
    const did = c.get("who").caller;
    const person = did.startsWith("did:") ? await rows.get("person/" + did) : null;
    if (!person) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "a member");
    const id = await idOf(did);
    return c.json({ did, id, methods: MEMBER_NS + id + ".", worker: `brain-m-${id}-NAME`, files: `u/${id}/`, tables: `m_${id}_NAME_`, quota: quotaOf(person), calls: (await rows.get(`mcalls/${did}/${today()}`)) || 0 });
  });
  app.get(NS + "member.services", async (c) => {
    const who = c.get("who").caller;
    if (who !== "owner" && !who.startsWith("did:")) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner or a member");
    // Another member's Worker is listed when one of its methods is for members.
    const shared = who !== "owner" && !!(await rows.get("person/" + who));
    const services = (await rows.list("route/")).map((r) => r.value).filter((r) => r.role === "member" && (who === "owner" || r.author === who || (shared && Object.values(r.methods).some((m) => m.who === "members"))));
    return c.json({ services: services.map((r) => ({ worker: r.worker, author: r.author, module: r.module, hash: r.hash, off: !!r.off, methods: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(r.methods).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.who])) })) });
  });
  // The owner's switch. Off: nothing reaches the Worker and it reaches nothing.
  app.post(NS + "member.switch", session, async (c) => {
    const { worker, off } = await c.req.json();
    const route = await rows.get("route/" + worker);
    if (!route || route.role !== "member") return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", String(worker));
    await settings.put("route/" + worker, { ...route, off: !!off });
    return c.json({ worker, off: !!off });
  });
  // A member's Worker is not listed here: the page loads the module of every Worker this names, as whoever is
  // signed in. member.services lists them.
  app.get(NS + "service.list", async (c) => c.json({ services: (await rows.list("route/")).map((r) => r.value).filter((r) => r.role !== "member") }));
  // The page's verdict on a deploy, after it ran the module's tests. A pass marks the hash verified. A fail while
  // the hash is still unverified has the deployer put the version before back; a fail after that is only recorded.
  app.post(NS + "deploy.report", owner, async (c) => {
    const { worker, hash, ok, tests = [], reason = "" } = await c.req.json();
    const route = await rows.get("route/" + worker);
    if (!route || !route.hash || route.hash !== hash) return fail(c, 409, "Stale", `${worker} is not running ${String(hash).slice(0, 12)}`);
    const was = route.verified;
    const failed = tests.filter((t) => !t.ok).map((t) => t.name);
    const verdict = { ok: !!ok, at: Date.now(), tests: tests.length, failed, reason: String(reason).slice(0, 300) };
    if (ok) {
      await settings.put("route/" + worker, { ...route, verified: verdict });
      // Every pass is passed on: the same hash deployed again is on probation again, and only the deployer knows.
      await toDeployer({ worker, hash, ok: true });
      return c.json({ worker, hash, state: "verified" });
    }
    if (was && was.ok) {
      await settings.put("route/" + worker, { ...route, failing: verdict });
      return c.json({ worker, hash, state: "failing" });
    }
    await settings.put("route/" + worker, { ...route, verified: verdict });
    const out = await toDeployer({ worker, hash, ok: false, reason: verdict.reason || "failed: " + failed.join(", ") });
    return c.json({ worker, hash, state: out && out.state === "put-back" ? "put-back" : "failed", previous: out ? out.previous || null : null });
  });

  // Rules the owner sets without a deploy. The target is a method's NSID or a path as its service declared it.
  // Only for what a Worker declared, and not for a method its service marked fixed (secret.*). The core's own
  // methods (rule.*, service.*) are decided in this file.
  const declared = async (target) => {
    for (const { value: r } of await rows.list("route/")) {
      if (!routed(r)) continue;
      if (r.methods[target]) return { worker: r.worker, rule: r.methods[target] };
      const p = r.paths.find((x) => x.path === target);
      if (p) return { worker: r.worker, rule: p };
    }
    return null;
  };
  app.get(NS + "rule.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const set = new Map((await rows.list("rule/")).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice("rule/".length), value]));
    const out = [];
    for (const { value: r } of await rows.list("route/")) {
      if (!routed(r)) continue;
      for (const [target, rule] of [...Object.entries(r.methods), ...r.paths.map((p) => [p.path, p])])
        out.push({ target, worker: r.worker, declared: ruleExpression(rule), set: set.has(target) ? set.get(target).allow : null, setAt: set.has(target) ? set.get(target).setAt : null });
    }
    return c.json({ rules: out.sort((a, b) => (a.target < b.target ? -1 : 1)), ttl: settings.ttl });
  });
  app.post(NS + "rule.put", session, async (c) => {
    const { target, allow } = await c.req.json();
    if (typeof allow !== "string" || !allow.trim()) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "allow is a CEL expression");
    const found = await declared(target);
    if (!found) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", `no service declares ${target}`);
    if (found.rule.fixed) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${found.worker} fixed the rule for ${target}`);
    // A rule that does not parse is refused here, not found on the next call.
    try {
      checkedRule(target, allow);
    } catch (e) {
      return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", e.message);
    }
    await settings.put("rule/" + target, { allow, setAt: Date.now() });
    return c.json({ target, allow });
  });
  app.post(NS + "rule.delete", session, async (c) => {
    const { target } = await c.req.json();
    return c.json({ deleted: !!(await settings.delete("rule/" + target)) });
  });

  // Settings: values a service reads from config with a default, stored per Worker and sent with each call forwarded
  // to it (see forward). Names the deployer binds, or that the kernel, the core or the deployer read, are refused.
  const PROTECTED = ["owner", "host", "base", "subdomain", "account", "deployer", "self", "replacedBy", "acceptEmitted", "probationMs", "clockSkewMs", "contextMs"];
  app.get(NS + "config.list", session, async (c) =>
    c.json({ workers: (await rows.list("config/")).map(({ key, value }) => ({ worker: key.slice("config/".length), values: value })), protected: PROTECTED, ttl: config.settingsMs ?? 60000 })
  );
  app.get(NS + "config.get", session, async (c) => {
    const worker = c.req.query("worker") || "", short = worker.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "");
    const route = await rows.get("route/" + worker);
    if (!route || !routed(route)) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", `no Worker ${worker} takes settings`);
    const values = (await rows.get("config/" + worker)) || {};
    // One running instance says what it has read. Another instance may have read more.
    const read = workers.has(short)
      ? await workers.fetch(short, new Request(`https://${short}.internal/xrpc/_config`, { headers: { "x-brain-settings": encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(values)) } })).then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : null), () => null)
      : null;
    return c.json({ worker, values, changes: (await rows.get("config-log/" + worker)) || [], read: read && Array.isArray(read.read) ? read.read : null });
  });
  app.post(NS + "config.set", session, async (c) => {
    const { worker, key, value = null } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    const route = typeof worker === "string" ? await rows.get("route/" + worker) : null;
    if (!route || !routed(route)) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", `no Worker ${worker} takes settings`);
    if (typeof key !== "string" || !/^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]{0,63}$/.test(key)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "key is a name of letters and digits");
    if (PROTECTED.includes(key)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", `${key} is set at deploy and is not a setting`);
    const plain = value === null || typeof value === "boolean" || (typeof value === "number" && Number.isFinite(value)) || (typeof value === "string" && value.length <= 500);
    if (!plain) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "value is a number, a boolean, text of at most 500 characters, or null to remove the key");
    const values = (await rows.get("config/" + worker)) || {};
    const old = Object.hasOwn(values, key) ? values[key] : null;
    if (value === null) delete values[key];
    else values[key] = value;
    if (Object.keys(values).length > 50) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "a Worker has at most 50 settings");
    // They travel as one header on every forwarded call.
    if (encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(values)).length > 8192) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "a Worker's settings are at most 8 KB as sent");
    if (Object.keys(values).length) await rows.put("config/" + worker, values);
    else await rows.delete("config/" + worker);
    stored = null;
    const change = { at: Date.now(), by: c.get("who").caller, key, old, value };
    await rows.append("config-log/" + worker, change, 100);
    console.log({ ...change, at: "config", worker });
    return c.json({ worker, key, value, old });
  });

  // The notebook side of the rows platform cell, one table per Worker name.
  const rowKey = (c, q) => "rows/" + (q.worker || "") + "/" + (q.key ?? q.prefix ?? "");
  app.get(NS + "rows.get", owner, async (c) => c.json({ value: await rows.get(rowKey(c, c.req.query())) }));
  app.get(NS + "rows.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const q = c.req.query(), base = "rows/" + (q.worker || "") + "/";
    return c.json({ rows: (await rows.list(base + (q.prefix || ""))).map(({ key, value }) => ({ key: key.slice(base.length), value })) });
  });
  app.post(NS + "rows.put", owner, async (c) => {
    const q = await c.req.json();
    return c.json({ ok: await rows.put(rowKey(c, q), q.value) });
  });
  app.post(NS + "rows.delete", owner, async (c) => c.json({ deleted: await rows.delete(rowKey(c, await c.req.json())) }));

  // getInfo for a named Worker, then everything a Worker declared.
  // A body of a known small size is read before it is sent on. A stream that the next Worker does not read to its end
  // throws "Can't read from request stream after response has been sent" here once the answer is out (cb4, 2026-10-08).
  // Every Worker's stored settings, read at most once in 60 s for this instance. config.set drops this instance's copy.
  let stored = null, storedAt = 0;
  const settingsOf = async (worker) => {
    if (!stored || Date.now() - storedAt >= (config.settingsMs ?? 60000)) {
      stored = new Map((await rows.list("config/")).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice("config/".length), value]));
      storedAt = Date.now();
    }
    return stored.get(worker) || {};
  };
  const bodyOf = async (c) => (+(c.req.header("content-length") || Infinity) <= 1e6 ? c.req.raw.arrayBuffer() : c.req.raw.body);
  const forward = async (route, c, path) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), who = c.get("who");
    const person = who.caller.startsWith("did:") ? await rows.get("person/" + who.caller) : null;
    const short = route.worker.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "");
    c.set("target", route.worker);
    if (!workers.has(short)) return fail(c, 502, "UpstreamUnavailable", `${route.worker} is not bound to the core`);
    const headers = new Headers(c.req.raw.headers);
    const ray = c.req.header("x-brain-ray");
    for (const name of [...headers.keys()]) if (name.startsWith("x-brain-")) headers.delete(name);
    headers.set("x-brain-caller", who.caller);
    if (who.via) headers.set("x-brain-via", who.via);
    // The caller's own tab, and who holds the delegation a call is under: a store keeps what such a call makes apart.
    headers.set("x-brain-tab", tabOf(who) ? "1" : "0");
    if (who.holder) headers.set("x-brain-holder", who.holder);
    if (ray) headers.set("x-brain-ray", ray);
    // The origin in clear, for a Worker that decides rules of its own, and the reference it sends back on a call it makes for this one.
    const origin = c.get("origin");
    headers.set("x-brain-origin", origin.caller);
    if (origin.via) headers.set("x-brain-origin-via", origin.via);
    headers.set("x-brain-origin-tab", tabOf(origin) ? "1" : "0");
    if (origin.holder) headers.set("x-brain-origin-holder", origin.holder);
    // How long the chain is. A holder that pushes on from this call sends it back, so a loop of pushes ends.
    headers.set("x-brain-hops", String(origin.hops || 0));
    headers.set("x-brain-context", await contextFor(route.worker, origin));
    // The Worker's stored settings. Always sent, so a removed key is seen as removed.
    headers.set("x-brain-settings", encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(await settingsOf(route.worker))));
    // What a store needs to decide for a person: that they are a member, their file limit and the tags they were granted.
    if (person) {
      headers.set("x-brain-member", "1");
      headers.set("x-brain-quota-bytes", String(quotaOf(person).bytes));
      headers.set("x-brain-tags", JSON.stringify(person.tags || []));
    }
    const bodied = !["GET", "HEAD"].includes(c.req.method);
    return workers.fetch(short, new Request("https://" + short + ".internal" + (path || url.pathname + url.search), { method: c.req.method, headers, body: bodied ? await bodyOf(c) : undefined, duplex: bodied ? "half" : undefined, redirect: "manual" }));
  };
  // Prices and credits. A method or a path may have a price: one CEL expression over the caller, the origin and the
  // request, which gives US dollars. The owner's price (price.put) stands in for the one a service declared. A call
  // with no price takes none of this. A priced call is charged to the account of its origin before it is forwarded,
  // and is refused when that leaves the account over its allowance for the UTC day.
  // An account's day is one row: a list that each charge is appended to, in one statement.
  // A charge counts when the charges that count before it, with it, are inside the allowance it was made under. That
  // is decided by the list alone, so calls made at once cannot spend past the allowance, and no call needs a lock.
  const PRICING = { owner: 1, member: 0.1, worker: 0.1, token: 0.1, perCall: 1, keepDays: 30 };
  const MICRO = 1e6, CHARGES = 2000, KEEP = 100000;
  const micro = (usd) => Math.ceil(usd * MICRO - 1e-6);
  const usd = (u) => u / MICRO;
  const pricing = async () => ({ ...PRICING, ...((await settings.get("quota/defaults")) || {}) });
  const accountOf = (origin) => {
    const o = callerOf(origin);
    return o.kind === "owner" || ["did", "token", "worker"].includes(o.kind) ? o.id : null;
  };
  const kindOf = (account) => (account === "owner" ? "owner" : account.startsWith("did:") ? "member" : account.split(":")[0]);
  const allowanceOf = async (account, p) => {
    const set = (await settings.list("quota/who/")).find((r) => r.key === "quota/who/" + account)?.value;
    return set && Number.isFinite(set.daily) ? set.daily : p[kindOf(account)] ?? 0;
  };
  const priceSet = async (target) => (await settings.list("price/")).find((r) => r.key === "price/" + target)?.value || null;
  const parsedPrice = new Map();
  const priceValue = (expression, context) => {
    try {
      if (!parsedPrice.has(expression)) parsedPrice.set(expression, cel.parse(expression));
      const v = parsedPrice.get(expression)(context), n = typeof v === "bigint" ? Number(v) : v;
      if (typeof n !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(n)) return { error: "it is not a number" };
      return n < 0 ? { error: "it is less than 0" } : { usd: n };
    } catch (e) {
      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e).split("\n")[0] };
    }
  };
  // What a day's list comes to: what is spent, and the charges that count.
  const fold = (list) => {
    let spent = 0;
    const net = new Map();
    for (const e of list || []) if (net.size < CHARGES && spent + e.u <= e.A) (net.set(e.i, e.u), (spent += e.u));
    return { spent, net, full: net.size >= CHARGES };
  };
  const spendKey = (day, account) => `spend/${day}/${account}`;
  // What this instance last read for an account. Spending only grows in a day, so an account read as spent is refused with no write.
  const known = new Map();
  const charge = async (account, u, allowance, about) => {
    const day = today(), key = spendKey(day, account), A = micro(allowance), k = known.get(account);
    if (k && k.day === day && (k.full || k.spent + u > A)) return { ok: false, spent: k.spent, full: k.full };
    const i = crypto.randomUUID().slice(0, 13);
    await rows.append(key, { t: Date.now(), i, u, A, ...about }, KEEP);
    const { spent, net, full } = fold(await rows.get(key));
    known.set(account, { day, spent, full });
    return { ok: net.has(i), spent, full: full && !net.has(i) };
  };
  let pruned = "";
  const prune = async (keepDays) => {
    if (pruned === today()) return;
    pruned = today();
    const dayAgo = (d) => new Date(clock() - d * 86400000);
    // 31 days by name, then the month of the last of them and 12 before it: a Brain with no priced call for a year still loses its old days.
    for (let d = keepDays + 1; d <= keepDays + 31; d++) await rows.deletePrefix(`spend/${dayAgo(d).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}/`);
    const edge = dayAgo(keepDays + 31);
    for (let m = 0; m <= 12; m++) await rows.deletePrefix(`spend/${new Date(Date.UTC(edge.getUTCFullYear(), edge.getUTCMonth() - m, 1)).toISOString().slice(0, 7)}-`);
  };
  const midnight = () => new Date(today() + "T00:00:00Z").getTime() + 86400000;
  const money = (n) => "$" + String(Number(n.toFixed(6)));
  const priced = async (c, route, target, rule, context) => {
    const set = await priceSet(target), expression = set ? set.price : rule.price;
    if (!expression) return forward(route, c);
    const p = await pricing(), price = priceValue(expression, context);
    if (price.error) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `the price of ${target} could not be decided: ${price.error}`);
    c.set("price", price.usd);
    if (price.usd > p.perCall) return fail(c, 402, "PriceOverCeiling", `${target} costs ${money(price.usd)} for this call. The most one call may cost is ${money(p.perCall)}`);
    const u = micro(price.usd);
    if (!u) return forward(route, c);
    const origin = c.get("origin"), account = accountOf(origin);
    if (!account) return fail(c, 402, "OutOfCredits", `${target} costs ${money(price.usd)} and ${callerOf(origin).id} has no credits`);
    if (!workers.has(route.worker.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, ""))) return forward(route, c);
    const allowance = await allowanceOf(account, p);
    // A chain under a delegation with a daily amount: refused when what it has spent, with this, is over the amount.
    // Its count is written after the account has paid, so a call the account refused is not in it. The cost of that
    // order: calls made at the same moment can each read the count before any is written, and pass the amount.
    const held = origin.d ? await settings.get("delegation/" + origin.d) : null, capped = held && Number.isFinite(held.daily);
    if (capped) {
      const { spent } = fold(await rows.get(spendKey(today(), "delegation/" + held.id)));
      if (spent + u > micro(held.daily)) return fail(c, 402, "OutOfCredits", `${target} costs ${money(usd(u))}. Delegation ${held.name} has spent ${money(usd(spent))} of ${money(held.daily)} today`);
    }
    const got = await charge(account, u, allowance, { m: target, c: c.get("who").caller, o: origin.caller, v: origin.via || "" });
    if (got.ok && capped) await rows.append(spendKey(today(), "delegation/" + held.id), { t: Date.now(), i: crypto.randomUUID().slice(0, 13), u, A: Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER, m: target }, KEEP);
    if (!got.ok)
      return fail(c, 402, "OutOfCredits", got.full
        ? `${account} has made ${CHARGES} priced calls today, which is the most for one day. The count is new at 00:00 UTC`
        : `${target} costs ${money(usd(u))}. ${account} has spent ${money(usd(got.spent))} of ${money(allowance)} today. The allowance is new at 00:00 UTC, in ${Math.ceil((midnight() - clock()) / 60000)} minutes`);
    const old = prune(p.keepDays).catch(() => null);
    try {
      c.executionCtx.waitUntil(old);
    } catch {}
    // The charge stands whatever the Worker answers.
    const r = await forward(route, c), out = new Response(r.body, r);
    out.headers.set("x-brain-price", String(usd(u)));
    return out;
  };
  // One account's day as the owner reads it. A charge that does not count was refused, and cost nothing.
  const ledgerOf = (who, list) => {
    const { net } = fold(list);
    return (list || []).filter((e) => e.u != null).map((e) => ({ at: e.t, who, origin: e.o + (e.v ? " (" + e.v + ")" : ""), caller: e.c, method: e.m, price: usd(e.u), cost: net.has(e.i) ? usd(e.u) : 0, counted: net.has(e.i) }));
  };
  const isAccount = (who) => who === "owner" || /^(did|token|worker):[^\s/]+$/.test(who || "");
  const dayOf = async (account, p, day = today()) => {
    const { spent } = fold(await rows.get(spendKey(day, account))), daily = await allowanceOf(account, p);
    return { who: account, day, spent: usd(spent), daily, remaining: Math.max(0, Number((daily - usd(spent)).toFixed(6))), resetsAt: midnight() };
  };
  app.get(NS + "price.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const set = new Map((await rows.list("price/")).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice("price/".length), value]));
    const out = [];
    for (const { value: r } of await rows.list("route/")) {
      if (!routed(r)) continue;
      for (const [target, rule] of [...Object.entries(r.methods), ...r.paths.map((p) => [p.path, p])])
        if (rule.price || set.has(target)) out.push({ target, worker: r.worker, declared: rule.price || null, set: set.has(target) ? set.get(target).price : null, setAt: set.has(target) ? set.get(target).setAt : null });
    }
    return c.json({ prices: out.sort((a, b) => (a.target < b.target ? -1 : 1)), unit: "USD", defaults: await pricing() });
  });
  app.post(NS + "price.put", session, async (c) => {
    const b = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({})), target = b.target || b.method, price = b.price;
    if (typeof price !== "string" || !price.trim()) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "price is a CEL expression that gives US dollars");
    const found = await declared(target);
    if (!found) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", `no service declares ${target}`);
    try {
      checkedRule(target, price);
    } catch (e) {
      return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", e.message.replace("the rule", "the price"));
    }
    await settings.put("price/" + target, { price, setAt: Date.now() });
    return c.json({ target, price });
  });
  app.post(NS + "price.delete", session, async (c) => {
    const b = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    return c.json({ deleted: !!(await settings.delete("price/" + (b.target || b.method))) });
  });
  // An account reads its own day. The owner reads any.
  app.get(NS + "quota.get", async (c) => {
    const who = c.get("who"), asked = c.req.query("who"), mine = accountOf(c.get("origin"));
    if (asked && asked !== mine && who.caller !== "owner") return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner reads another account");
    if (!(asked || mine)) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "an account");
    if (asked && !isAccount(asked)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "who is owner, did:…, token:NAME or worker:NAME");
    return c.json(await dayOf(asked || mine, await pricing()));
  });
  app.get(NS + "quota.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const p = await pricing(), day = today(), base = `spend/${day}/`;
    const set = new Map((await rows.list("quota/who/")).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice("quota/who/".length), value]));
    // A delegation's own count is under delegation/<id>: delegation.list shows it, and it is no account.
    const spent = new Map((await rows.list(base)).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice(base.length), value]).filter(([who]) => !who.startsWith("delegation/")));
    // The owner, each account with an allowance of its own, and each that has spent today. One whose every charge was refused is in the ledger only.
    const accounts = [...new Set(["owner", ...set.keys(), ...spent.keys()])].sort().map((who) => {
      const daily = set.has(who) && Number.isFinite(set.get(who).daily) ? set.get(who).daily : p[kindOf(who)] ?? 0;
      return { who, daily, set: set.has(who), spent: usd(fold(spent.get(who)).spent), charges: (spent.get(who) || []).filter((e) => e.u != null).length };
    }).filter((a) => a.who === "owner" || a.set || a.spent > 0);
    return c.json({ day, unit: "USD", resetsAt: midnight(), defaults: p, accounts });
  });
  app.post(NS + "quota.put", session, async (c) => {
    const { who, daily = null } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    if (!isAccount(who)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "who is owner, did:…, token:NAME or worker:NAME");
    if (daily !== null && !(typeof daily === "number" && Number.isFinite(daily) && daily >= 0)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "daily is US dollars, 0 or more, or null for the default");
    if (daily === null) await settings.delete("quota/who/" + who);
    else await settings.put("quota/who/" + who, { daily, setAt: Date.now() });
    return c.json(await dayOf(who, await pricing()));
  });
  app.post(NS + "quota.setDefaults", session, async (c) => {
    const b = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({})), next = { ...((await rows.get("quota/defaults")) || {}) };
    for (const k of Object.keys(PRICING)) {
      if (!(k in b)) continue;
      if (b[k] === null) delete next[k];
      else if (typeof b[k] === "number" && Number.isFinite(b[k]) && b[k] >= 0 && (k !== "keepDays" || (Number.isInteger(b[k]) && b[k] >= 1))) next[k] = b[k];
      else return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", `${k} is a number, 0 or more, or null for ${PRICING[k]}`);
    }
    await settings.put("quota/defaults", next);
    return c.json({ defaults: await pricing() });
  });
  app.get(NS + "quota.ledger", owner, async (c) => {
    const day = c.req.query("day") || today(), who = c.req.query("who");
    if (!/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/.test(day)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "day is YYYY-MM-DD");
    if (who && !isAccount(who)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "who is owner, did:…, token:NAME or worker:NAME");
    const base = `spend/${day}/`;
    // Not the delegations' own counts: each of those charges is in its account's list too.
    const lists = who ? [[who, await rows.get(base + who)]] : (await rows.list(base)).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice(base.length), value]).filter(([w]) => !w.startsWith("delegation/"));
    const charges = lists.flatMap(([w, list]) => ledgerOf(w, list)).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at);
    const sum = (by) => Object.entries(charges.reduce((t, e) => ((t[e[by]] = (t[e[by]] || 0) + e.cost), t), {})).map(([k, v]) => ({ [by]: k, cost: Number(v.toFixed(6)) }));
    return c.json({ day, unit: "USD", charges: charges.slice(0, Math.min(2000, Number(c.req.query("limit")) || 200)), total: Number(charges.reduce((t, e) => t + e.cost, 0).toFixed(6)), byWho: sum("who"), byMethod: sum("method") });
  });

  // /llms.txt: how a program calls this Brain, for anyone. Written from config.host and the route table on each
  // request, so a clone and a newly deployed service are right with no edit. It points at each Worker's own reference
  // (getSource) and copies none of it. A member's Worker is left out, and so is what the owner set in place of a
  // declared rule or price: only that one was set.
  app.get("/llms.txt", async (c) => {
    const at = "https://" + config.host, X = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.";
    const dep = typeof config.deployer === "string" ? config.deployer.replace(/\/+$/, "") : "";
    const set = new Set([...(await settings.list("rule/")), ...(await settings.list("price/"))].map((r) => r.key.replace(/^(rule|price)\//, "")));
    const line = (name, r, kind) => `- ${name}: ${kind}${r.allow ? "by its rule" : r.who || "owner"}${r.price ? ", has a price" : ""}${set.has(name) ? ", changed by the owner" : ""}`;
    const routes = (await settings.list("route/")).map((r) => r.value).filter((r) => routed(r) && r.role !== "member").sort((a, b) => (a.worker < b.worker ? -1 : 1));
    const deployed = routes.filter((r) => Object.keys(r.methods).length + r.paths.length).map((r) => [`### ${r.worker}`, ...Object.entries(r.methods).sort().map(([n, m]) => line(n, m, m.type + ", ")), ...r.paths.map((p) => line(p.path, p, "path, "))].join("\n"));
    // Said only where a Worker declares the method: a clone with no knowledge base is told of none.
    const holds = routes.some((r) => "com.lopecode.brain.knowledge.search" in r.methods) ? `
## Finding what it holds

- \`GET ${at}${X}knowledge.search?semantic=true&q=<the task, in words>\`: what this Brain holds that is nearest the question, as pointers (\`title\`, \`kind\`, \`url\`, \`id\`): notebook modules (\`&kind=module\`), the docs of how the notebooks and this Brain are worked on (\`&kind=doc\`), papers, articles, notes. Search here before writing something that may exist. The owner or a token that names the method; \`knowledge.get?id=\` has an entry's text.
` : "";
    const text = `# Cloud Brain at ${at}

Cloudflare Workers that one notebook defines, deploys and operates. This file is written on each request from what is deployed here. It points at the reference and copies none of it.

## Calling

- A method is ${at}/xrpc/<name>, with the whole name as it is listed under Deployed.
- query: GET with query parameters. procedure: POST with a JSON body.
- A refusal is JSON \`{ error, message }\`: 401 \`AuthRequired\` (the rule is not true for this caller), 403 \`Forbidden\`, 402 (the call has a price), 501 (nothing declares the method).
- With no \`Authorization\` header the caller is \`anonymous\`. Methods marked \`anyone\` answer it.

## A token, for a caller with no browser

- The owner makes one in a signed-in session: POST ${at}${X}token.create with \`{ "name": "laptop", "methods": ["com.lopecode.brain.knowledge.search"] }\`. The answer shows the token once.
- Or the owner makes a sign-in link (\`token.link\` with \`{ name, methods }\`, or the page) and pastes it to the program. A GET of the link says what to do; the first POST of it answers a token that lasts 8 hours, and the link is gone.
- A token calls the methods it names and no others. A name can be a prefix: \`browser.*\`, or \`*\` for every method of this Brain. It cannot name \`infra.*\`, \`secret.*\`, \`token.*\`, \`grant.*\` or \`people.*\`, and a method marked \`by its rule\` may refuse it; the reference says. The token of a sign-in link made with \`unattended\` is the exception: its calls are made as the owner's session, and the owner's allowance pays.
- Send it as \`Authorization: Bearer <token>\`. Not in a query string: paths and query strings are kept in the logs.
- \`token.list\`, and \`token.revoke\` with \`{ name }\`, are the owner's.

## From Claude Code on the web

- The session's environment must allow \`${config.host}\`: in the environment's settings set network access to custom and add that host (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cloud-environments, read 2026-10-09).
- A token from a sign-in link: keep it in a file of mode 600 in a temporary directory, outside the repository, since a shell command there does not keep a variable for the next one. A standing token: an environment variable of that environment, not the repository or the prompt.
- Use curl, or send a User-Agent of your own. Cloudflare refuses Python's urllib with 403 "error code: 1010" before this Brain sees the call (measured 2026-10-10: urllib refused; python-requests, node, Go and curl pass).
- \`curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $(jq -r .token <the file>)" "${at}${X}<a method the token names>"\`, or \`$BRAIN_TOKEN\` for a standing token in the environment.

## Finding your way

Three calls, with no account, say what this Brain is made of:

- \`GET ${at}${X}service.list\`: every Worker. For each: \`worker\`, the notebook \`module\` it is made from, \`role\`, \`methods\`, \`paths\`, and the \`hash\` of the code running. Start here.
- \`GET ${at}${X}getInfo?worker=<worker>\`: what one Worker declares: who may call each method (\`access\`), the methods of other Workers it \`calls\`, the names of its secrets, the platform cells it uses.
- \`GET ${at}${X}getSource?worker=<worker>\`: JSON \`{ worker, hash, module, text }\`. \`text\` is the whole module that Worker runs, as deployed: its code, its tests (\`test_\` cells) and its documentation (its \`md\` cells). \`hash\` is what a deploy of that module replaces.
- \`GET ${at}${X}getSource?worker=<worker>&part=reference\`: only the documentation, as text: that Worker's methods, inputs and answers. Read this before calling a method.

The shape: the kernel (\`brain\`) is this address and says who the caller is. The core (\`brain-core\`) checks the rule of each method, charges its price and passes the call to a service (\`brain-x-NAME\`). \`brain-db\` keeps every Worker's rows. The deployer, a Worker at its own address, is the only holder of a Cloudflare token: it deploys a module's source as a Worker and puts back one that fails. A service is one notebook module; its source is its definition.
${holds}
## Making a service

- A member of this Brain deploys their own: \`member.deploy\` with \`{ module, source, reason, was }\`. \`source\` is a module as \`getSource\` gives one. \`reason\` says why, in 3 to 300 characters, and is logged. \`was\` is the hash you saw running for that service, \`null\` for a new one; the deploy is refused when it is no longer that. No approval is needed. \`member.services\` lists them, \`member.remove\` takes \`{ name, reason, was }\`.
- The owner makes a DID a member with \`people.put\`. A member calls from a signed-in page, or from a program with a service token of their own PDS (\`com.atproto.server.getServiceAuth\`, \`aud\` \`did:web:${config.host}\`, \`lxm\` the method's whole name).
- A member's service has no secrets, no paths and no Cloudflare permissions, and its methods are \`com.lopecode.brain.m.<id>.<name>\`. The limits and the rules are in the deployer's reference${dep ? ` (\`GET ${dep}${X}getSource?part=reference\`)` : ""} and in \`getSource?worker=brain&part=reference\`.
- The owner deploys any Worker with \`infra.apply\`: in their own session, or with the token of a sign-in link they made with \`deploy\`. Body \`{ reason, workers: [{ module, source, was }] }\`: \`source\` is the module's text as \`getSource\` gives it, changed; \`was\` is the \`hash\` \`getSource\` gave. The answer has a \`state\` for each: \`deployed\`, \`probation\`, \`unchanged\`, \`refused\` with a \`reason\`, or \`waiting\`, which means the owner approves it on the deployer's page and the same call is then sent again (a token whose sign-in answer said \`"unattended": true\` is never made to wait). A service gets a Cloudflare API token of its own by declaring \`cloudflare: ["GROUP"]\` in its \`cloudflare.Service\` options; the deployer mints the groups on its own list and answers \`refused\`, with the reason, for another. After a deploy of the page module, a token that is \`unattended\` POSTs the notebook's HTML to \`infra.shell\`; another asks the owner to. A kernel, core or page is on \`probation\` and is put back in 10 minutes unless \`infra.confirm\` (POST, \`{}\`) is called once it answers. \`infra.getState\` says what runs. Any other token cannot.

## Reference

- \`GET ${at}${X}getSource?worker=<worker>&part=reference\`: that Worker's methods, inputs and answers, as text. Without \`part\`: JSON whose \`text\` is the whole module.
- The kernel, the core and the deployer have methods of their own, which are not listed under Deployed. \`worker=brain\` is the kernel (sign-in, tokens, grants, people). \`worker=brain-core\` is the core (rules, prices, quota, settings, members' services).${dep ? ` The deployer answers at its own address: \`GET ${dep}${X}getSource?part=reference\` (\`infra.*\`, \`member.deploy\`).` : ""}
- \`${at}/.well-known/did.json\`. \`quota.get\`: what this caller has spent today (a token must name it). \`${at}/\` is the notebook that defines all of this, for a person.

## Deployed

One section for each service, and the database. Each line: name, query or procedure, who the service says may call. \`by its rule\`: an expression of the service's own decides, and nothing else; its reference says what. \`owner\`: the owner, and a token or a member the owner gave the method. \`workers\`: those, and this Brain's own Workers. \`anyone\`: those, and a caller with no account. \`worker:NAME\`: the owner side, and that one Worker.

${deployed.join("\n\n")}
`;
    return c.text(text, 200, { "cache-control": "no-store", "access-control-allow-origin": "*" });
  });

  // A Worker's manifest and source, for anyone. The wrapper has already answered for the core itself.
  for (const what of ["getInfo", "getSource"])
    app.get(NS + what, async (c) => {
      const name = c.req.query("worker") || "brain-core";
      const route = await settings.get("route/" + name);
      if (!route || !routed(route) || route.role === "member") return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", name);
      return forward(route, c, NS + what + "?worker=" + encodeURIComponent(name) + (c.req.query("part") === "reference" ? "&part=reference" : ""));
    });
  // Making a delegation. The holder is a Worker the owner deployed, or a secret that this answers once: a token.
  // A secret is the owner's to make so far, and it alone has caps. A DID holder is the kernel's grant until that moves here.
  const CAPS = ["session", "deploy", "unattended"];
  const drop = async (d) => {
    await settings.delete("delegation/" + d.id);
    if (d.holder && d.holder.secret) await settings.delete("holder/secret/" + d.holder.secret);
  };
  app.post(NS + "delegation.create", inPerson, async (c) => {
    const from = c.get("who").caller, b = (await c.req.json().catch(() => null)) || {};
    const { name, holder, caps = [], until = null, daily = null, note = "" } = b;
    const one = holder && typeof holder === "object" && Object.keys(holder).length === 1, secretHeld = !!one && holder.secret === true;
    // A token may name no method: a sign-in link made only to deploy.
    const scope = secretHeld && Array.isArray(b.scope) && !b.scope.length ? [] : scoped(b.scope);
    if (typeof name !== "string" || !/^[a-z0-9-]{1,40}$/.test(name)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "name is a-z, 0-9 and -, 1 to 40 characters");
    if (!secretHeld && !(one && typeof holder.worker === "string")) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "holder is { worker: NAME } or { secret: true }");
    if (secretHeld && from !== "owner") return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "a secret holder is the owner's to make");
    // A delegation names a Worker and not its code, so the Worker is one the owner deploys.
    const route = secretHeld ? null : await rows.get("route/" + holder.worker);
    if (!secretHeld && (!route || !["recipe", "system"].includes(route.role))) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", `${holder.worker} is not a service the owner deployed`);
    if (!Array.isArray(caps) || caps.some((x) => !CAPS.includes(x)) || new Set(caps).size !== caps.length) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "caps are session, deploy and unattended");
    if (caps.length && !secretHeld) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "a Worker holder has no caps");
    // Deploying with nobody asked can deploy a kernel, so it is the owner in effect and is said to be: both other caps.
    if (caps.includes("unattended") && !(caps.includes("deploy") && caps.includes("session"))) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "unattended goes with deploy and session");
    if (!scope) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "scope is 1 to 50 method names; a prefix ends .* or /*, and * is every method");
    const no = scope.find(neverHeld);
    if (no) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", `${no} is not reached under a delegation`);
    if (from !== "owner") {
      const me = await rows.get("person/" + from), ALL = "com.lopecode.brain.*";
      const over = scope.find((m) => m !== ALL && !may({ member: true, grant: me.methods }, m) && !(/[./]\*$/.test(m) && MEMBER.some((own) => own.startsWith(m.slice(0, -1)))));
      if (over) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${from} may not call ${over}`);
    }
    if (until !== null && !(Number.isInteger(until) && until > clock())) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "until is a time in ms after now, or null");
    if (daily !== null && !(typeof daily === "number" && Number.isFinite(daily) && daily >= 0)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "daily is US dollars a UTC day, or null");
    if (typeof note !== "string" || note.length > 300) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "note is text, at most 300 characters");
    // What has ended goes when its maker makes another.
    const mine = (await rows.list("delegation/")).map((r) => r.value).filter((o) => o.from === from), live = [];
    for (const o of mine) o.until && o.until <= clock() ? await drop(o) : live.push(o.name);
    if (live.includes(name)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", `a delegation named ${name} exists; revoke it first`);
    const hex = (n) => [...crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(n))].map((x) => x.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
    const id = hex(6), secret = secretHeld ? hex(32) : null;
    const d = { id, name, from, holder: secretHeld ? { secret: await sha256(secret) } : { worker: holder.worker }, scope, caps, until, daily, parent: null, note, created: Date.now(), by: c.get("who").via };
    await settings.put("delegation/" + id, d);
    if (secret) await settings.put("holder/secret/" + d.holder.secret, id);
    // The secret is in this answer and nowhere else: the row has its hash.
    return c.json(secret ? { ...d, secret } : d);
  });
  // The owner reads every delegation, a member their own. spentToday: what was charged under it this UTC day.
  app.get(NS + "delegation.list", inPerson, async (c) => {
    const me = c.get("who").caller, day = today();
    const mine = (await rows.list("delegation/")).map((r) => r.value).filter((d) => me === "owner" || d.from === me).sort((a, b) => a.created - b.created);
    return c.json({ delegations: await Promise.all(mine.map(async (d) => ({ ...d, spentToday: usd(fold(await rows.get(spendKey(day, "delegation/" + d.id))).spent) }))) });
  });
  app.post(NS + "delegation.revoke", inPerson, async (c) => {
    const me = c.get("who").caller, { id } = (await c.req.json().catch(() => null)) || {};
    const d = typeof id === "string" && /^[0-9a-f]{12}$/.test(id) ? await rows.get("delegation/" + id) : null;
    if (!d || (me !== "owner" && d.from !== me)) return c.json({ revoked: false });
    await drop(d);
    return c.json({ revoked: true, id });
  });
  // A token from before 2026-10-10 was a row of the kernel, which has the hash of its secret and not the secret.
  // The kernel hands each over once. A name one of the owner's delegations has is kept apart by the new id.
  app.post(NS + "delegation.adopt", async (c) => {
    const w = c.get("who"), b = (await c.req.json().catch(() => null)) || {};
    if (!(w.kernel && w.caller === "kernel")) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the kernel");
    const ok = typeof b.sha256 === "string" && /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(b.sha256) && typeof b.name === "string" && /^[a-z0-9-]{1,40}$/.test(b.name) && Array.isArray(b.scope) && b.scope.every((m) => typeof m === "string") && Array.isArray(b.caps) && b.caps.every((x) => CAPS.includes(x));
    if (!ok) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "{ sha256, name, scope, caps, until, created, note }");
    const had = await rows.get("holder/secret/" + b.sha256);
    if (had && (await rows.get("delegation/" + had))) return c.json(await rows.get("delegation/" + had));
    const id = [...crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(6))].map((x) => x.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
    const taken = (await rows.list("delegation/")).some((r) => r.value.from === "owner" && r.value.name === b.name);
    const d = { id, name: taken ? b.name.slice(0, 35) + "-" + id.slice(0, 4) : b.name, from: "owner", holder: { secret: b.sha256 }, scope: b.scope, caps: b.caps, until: Number.isInteger(b.until) ? b.until : null, daily: null, parent: null, note: typeof b.note === "string" ? b.note.slice(0, 300) : "", created: Number.isInteger(b.created) ? b.created : Date.now(), by: "moved" };
    await settings.put("delegation/" + id, d);
    await settings.put("holder/secret/" + b.sha256, id);
    return c.json(d);
  });
  // The kernel asks whose secret it was sent: it needs the scope for the routes it answers itself and the caps for
  // infra.*. The row is found by the hash, and the answer has no secret in it.
  app.post(NS + "delegation.resolve", async (c) => {
    const w = c.get("who"), { sha256: hash } = (await c.req.json().catch(() => null)) || {};
    if (!(w.kernel && w.caller === "kernel")) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the kernel");
    // Read with no memory: anyone can send a bearer nobody made, and settings would keep an entry for each.
    const id = typeof hash === "string" && /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(hash) ? await rows.get("holder/secret/" + hash) : null;
    const d = id ? await settings.get("delegation/" + id) : null;
    return c.json({ delegation: d && d.holder.secret === hash ? d : null });
  });
  app.all("*", async (c) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), who = c.get("who");
    const { route, method, path, nsid } = await routeOf(c);
    if (route) {
      const rule = method || path;
      if (method && (method.type === "query") !== (c.req.method === "GET")) return fail(c, 405, "InvalidRequest", `${nsid} is a ${method.type}`);
      // A rule and a price read the query string as a map, which has the last of a name given two times. A service
      // may read the first. So that the two never read different values, such a call is refused.
      const given = [...url.searchParams.keys()];
      if (new Set(given).size !== given.length) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "a query parameter is given two times");
      // A member's Worker answers while its author is a member and the owner has not switched it off.
      if (route.role === "member") {
        const now = await rows.get("route/" + route.worker), person = await rows.get("person/" + route.author);
        if (!now || now.off) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${route.worker} is switched off`);
        if (!person) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${route.author} is not a member`);
        if (!(await spend(person))) return fail(c, 429, "RateLimitExceeded", `${route.author} has used today's ${quotaOf(person).calls} calls`);
      }
      // The rule is one CEL expression over the caller, the origin and the request. Anything but true is a refusal.
      // A rule the owner has set for this method or path stands in for the one the service declared.
      const set = (await settings.list("rule/")).find((r) => r.key === "rule/" + (nsid || path.path))?.value;
      const context = { caller: callerOf(who), origin: callerOf(c.get("origin")), request: { method: nsid || "", path: url.pathname, verb: c.req.method, params: Object.fromEntries(url.searchParams) } };
      const verdict = decide(set ? { allow: set.allow } : rule, context);
      c.set("rule", verdict.allow ? "allow" : verdict.error ? "error" : "deny");
      c.set("by", set ? "owner" : rule.fixed ? "fixed" : "manifest");
      // Allowed, then priced: a call with a price is charged to its origin's account before it is forwarded.
      if (verdict.allow) return priced(c, route, nsid || path.path, rule, context);
      return verdict.error ? fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "the rule for this could not be decided") : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "not allowed by the rule for this");
    }
    return nsid ? fail(c, 501, "MethodNotImplemented", nsid) : c.text("not found", 404);
  });
  return app;
}
// %%

md`## Tests

The core runs under \`simulate\`. \`coreRig\` registers a kernel and one recipe the way the deployer would, then calls as each kind of caller.`
// %%
coreRig = async ({ config = {}, workers: more = {} } = {}) => {
  const seen = [], toDeployer = [];
  // What brain-x-echo's own manifest says, as the wrapper would answer at getInfo.
  const echo = { hash: "h1", calls: ["com.lopecode.brain.other.*"] };
  const sim = await simulate(core_service, {
    secrets: { BRAIN_KEY: "core-key" },
    config,
    deployer: async (request) => {
      const body = await request.json();
      toDeployer.push({ path: new URL(request.url).pathname, key: request.headers.get("x-brain-key"), body });
      return Response.json(body.ok ? { state: "kept" } : { state: "put-back", previous: "h0" });
    },
    workers: {
      echo: async (request) => {
        if (request.url === "https://echo.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.getInfo") return Response.json({ name: "brain-x-echo", hash: echo.hash, calls: echo.calls });
        const body = ["GET", "HEAD"].includes(request.method) ? null : new TextDecoder().decode(await request.arrayBuffer());
        seen.push({ url: request.url, method: request.method, caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), cookie: request.headers.get("cookie"), key: request.headers.get("x-brain-key"), body });
        return request.url.includes("/redirect") ? new Response(null, { status: 302, headers: { location: "https://example.com/" } }) : Response.json({ echoed: new URL(request.url).pathname });
      },
      ...more
    }
  });
  const X = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.";
  const send = (base, headers) => async (path, body, extra = {}) => {
    const r = await sim.fetch(base + (path.startsWith("/") ? path : X + path), {
      method: body === undefined ? "GET" : "POST",
      headers: { ...headers, ...extra, ...(body === undefined ? {} : { "content-type": "application/json" }) },
      body: body === undefined ? undefined : typeof body === "string" || body instanceof Uint8Array ? body : JSON.stringify(body),
      redirect: "manual"
    });
    const text = await r.text();
    let data = text;
    try { data = JSON.parse(text); } catch {}
    return { status: r.status, data, headers: r.headers };
  };
  // Another Worker's answer to anything: it keeps who the core said was calling and for whom.
  const heard = [];
  const hear = (worker) => async (request) => (heard.push({ worker, caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), origin: request.headers.get("x-brain-origin"), via: request.headers.get("x-brain-origin-via"), context: request.headers.get("x-brain-context") }), Response.json({ ok: true }));
  const deployer = send("https://cb-core.sub.workers.dev", { "x-brain-deployer": "core-key" });
  const as = (caller, via = "session") => send("https://core.internal", { "x-brain-key": "kernel-key", "x-brain-caller": caller, "x-brain-via": via });
  const worker = send("https://core.internal", { "x-brain-key": "echo-key", "x-brain-caller": "owner" });
  await deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain", role: "kernel", methods: {}, paths: [], secrets: [], keyHash: await sha256("kernel-key") });
  await deployer("service.register", {
    worker: "brain-x-echo",
    role: "recipe",
    methods: { "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" }, "com.lopecode.brain.echo.read": { type: "query", who: "anyone" }, "com.lopecode.brain.echo.key": { type: "query", who: "owner", fixed: true } },
    paths: [{ path: "/hooks/echo", who: "anyone" }, { path: "/redirect", who: "anyone" }, { path: "/private", who: "owner" }],
    secrets: ["ECHO_KEY"],
    hash: "h1",
    module: "@tomlarkworthy/echo",
    keyHash: await sha256("echo-key")
  });
  return { sim, seen, toDeployer, deployer, as, worker, echo, heard, hear, send, owner: as("owner"), anonymous: as("anonymous", ""), nobody: send("https://core.internal", {}) };
}
// %%
test_llms_txt_is_written_from_the_host_and_the_route_table = {
  const rig = await coreRig({ config: { host: "clone.example.workers.dev", deployer: "https://clone-deployer.example.workers.dev" } });
  const read = async () => (await rig.anonymous("/llms.txt")).data;
  const first = await rig.anonymous("/llms.txt");
  expect(first.status).toBe(200);
  expect(first.headers.get("content-type")).toMatch(/^text\/plain/);
  // Every address is this Brain's own: a clone needs no edit.
  expect(first.data).toContain("# Cloud Brain at https://clone.example.workers.dev\n");
  expect(first.data.match(/https:\/\/[a-z0-9.-]+/g).filter((u) => !/^https:\/\/(clone(-deployer)?\.example\.workers\.dev|code\.claude\.com)$/.test(u))).toEqual([]);
  expect(first.data).toContain("### brain-x-echo\n- com.lopecode.brain.echo.key: query, owner\n- com.lopecode.brain.echo.read: query, anyone\n- com.lopecode.brain.echo.say: procedure, owner\n- /hooks/echo: path, anyone");
  expect(first.data).toContain("getSource?worker=<worker>&part=reference");
  // Where to begin, what getSource answers, and how a member makes a service.
  for (const said of ["service.list`: every Worker", "getInfo?worker=<worker>", "`{ worker, hash, module, text }`", "`member.deploy` with `{ module, source, reason, was }`", "`aud` `did:web:clone.example.workers.dev`"]) expect(first.data).toContain(said);
  // The knowledge base is pointed at only once a Worker declares its search.
  expect(first.data).not.toContain("Finding what it holds");
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-knowledge", role: "recipe", keyHash: "know", paths: [], secrets: [], methods: { "com.lopecode.brain.knowledge.search": { type: "query", who: "owner" } } });
  expect(await read()).toContain("## Finding what it holds\n\n- `GET https://clone.example.workers.dev/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.knowledge.search?semantic=true&q=<the task, in words>`");
  // Every name is whole, so it is the path: a listed name asked as listed is routed (not 501).
  expect(first.data).not.toContain("is short for");
  expect(first.data).toContain("https://clone-deployer.example.workers.dev/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.getSource?part=reference");
  // A service deployed later is listed, with its rule and price said to exist. Another lexicon's name is whole.
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-shop", role: "recipe", keyHash: "shop", paths: [], secrets: [], methods: { "com.lopecode.brain.shop.buy": { type: "procedure", who: "anyone", allow: "caller.session", price: "0.01" }, "app.bsky.feed.getFeedSkeleton": { type: "query", who: "anyone" } } });
  expect(await read()).toContain("### brain-x-shop\n- app.bsky.feed.getFeedSkeleton: query, anyone\n- com.lopecode.brain.shop.buy: procedure, by its rule, has a price");
  // What the owner set is not shown, only that it was. A member's Worker is not listed.
  await rig.owner("rule.put", { target: "com.lopecode.brain.echo.read", allow: 'caller.id == "did:plc:private"' });
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-m-ada-notes", role: "member", author: "did:plc:ada", keyHash: "ada", paths: [], secrets: [], methods: { "com.lopecode.brain.m.ada.notes.list": { type: "query", who: "anyone" } } });
  const last = await read();
  expect(last).toContain("- com.lopecode.brain.echo.read: query, anyone, changed by the owner");
  expect(last).not.toContain("did:plc:");
  expect(last).not.toContain("brain-m-ada");
  // The reference of one Worker is asked of that Worker.
  await rig.anonymous("getSource?worker=brain-x-echo&part=reference");
  expect(rig.seen.at(-1).url).toBe("https://echo.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.getSource?worker=brain-x-echo&part=reference");
  return last.length + " characters";
}
